              Digital Delivers Next Wave of Wi ndows NT
                       Integration for OpenVMS
              
    New Products for System Management, World Wide Web Hosting,
       Enterprise Messaging and Application Development Build
  on the Affinity Between OpenVMS and Windows NT; Software Vendors
           Respond to User Demand with Applications, Tools

      ST. LOUIS, Mo. -- June 3, 1996 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation and its business partners today announced the second 
wave of products and services that allow OpenVMS customers to 
integrate Microsoft Windows NT easily into their enterprise 
computing environments. Today's expansion of the OpenVMS and
Windows NT affinity program further streamlines customers' ability 
to bring the proven mission-critical capabilities of OpenVMS to 
Windows NT applications, and simplifies the deployment and 
management of applications across both platforms.

     Announced today at the Digital Equipment Computer User Society 
(DECUS) conference in St. Louis on June 1-6, 1996 are the following 
products, services and partnerships.

     o System and network management: OpenVMS Management Tools for 
       Windows NT V1.0, POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows    
       NT V3.1 and POLYCENTER Capacity Planner for Windows NT V3.0, 
       enabling OpenVMS and Windows NT systems to be managed from    
       Windows NT

     o World Wide Web hosting: OpenVMS Internet Product Suite v1.0 
       and ALL-IN-1 Office Server V3.2 for OpenVMS, enabling 	   
       OpenVMS users to participate fully on the Web 

     o Integrated enterprise messaging: MAILbus 400 Message 	   
       Transfer Agent V2.0, MAILbus Monitor V2.0, Digital X.500    
       Directory Services V3.0 and support for the Defense 	   
       Messaging System

     o C++ application development: Application Developers Package 
       V1.0, for simplified OpenVMS and Windows NT integration

     o Software tools and applications: support from 32 software    
       vendors, bringing to nearly 60 the number of partners 	   
       supporting OpenVMS and Windows NT integration today

     o Support services: a suite of services from Digital    
       Multivendor Customer Services

     "Through Digital's ongoing delivery of the OpenVMS and Windows 
NT affinity program, customers can, with increasing ease, integrate 
application-rich Windows NT servers with back-end OpenVMS servers 
and Windows desktop clients.  This three-tier client/server 
approach enables development of Windows applications with 24-hour, 
365-day availability, disaster tolerance and nearly unlimited 
scaleability," said Wes Melling, OpenVMS System Group vice 
president. "We have given OpenVMS customers a clear action plan for
integrating Windows NT, and we are backing that plan with the tools 
they need.  This approach ensures that our customers are 
best-prepared to invest in Windows NT software for mission-critical 
computing."

Delivering Integrated System and Network Management

     A key capability of Digital's program is to enable OpenVMS and 
Windows NT systems on a global network to be managed from a Windows 
NT station. This allows customers to manage the large-scale 
deployment of integrated OpenVMS and Windows NT environments.
OpenVMS Management Tools for Windows NT V1.0 

     OpenVMS Management Tools for Windows NT simplifies management 
of OpenVMS user and system accounts, printers and print queues, all 
from a Windows NT system.  The software is licensed as part of the 
OpenVMS operating system and is available in July.
POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT V3.1

     POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT V3.1 sets new 
standards for enterprise management from Windows NT. Performance 
benchmarks conducted with the assistance of noted industry analyst 
Jill Huntington-Lee, formerly of Datapro Information Services Group 
in Delran, N.J., proved that V3.1 manages more than 8,000 nodes 
from an Intel-based PC and more than 13,000 nodes from a Digital 
Alpha system.

     POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT V3.1 is priced at 
$6,995 and is available immediately.
POLYCENTER Capacity Planner for Windows NT V3.0

     POLYCENTER Capacity Planner is a system and network sizing 
tool that helps predict  how applications will perform in a 
production environment. It features "what-if" modeling capabilities 
for determining optimum system and network design. POLYCENTER 
Capacity Planner for Windows NT is priced at $2,000 and is 
available in July.

Delivering Secure, Reliable World Wide Web Hosting

     With OpenVMS Internet Product Suite V1.0, Digital delivers a 
comprehensive collection of leading Internet products and freeware 
in a convenient CD-ROM package. The suite enables customers to 
bring OpenVMS's strengths as a secure, continuous-computing 
platform to their World Wide Web applications. It provides 
everything customers need to deploy OpenVMS systems as Web servers 
or clients in the three-tier client/server environment. Included 
are the following.

Commercial Web Browsers

     OpenVMS Internet Product Suite offers a choice of Web browsers 
for OpenVMS: Netscape Navigator V2.0, with support for JavaScript; 
and Spyglass Enhanced Mosaic V2.10, with support for HTML 
extensions.

Commercial Web Servers

     Web server software for Internet and intranet development on 
OpenVMS includes Netscape Communications Server V1.12 and Purveyor 
WebServer for OpenVMS V1.1B.  Also offered is Netscape Commerce 
Server V1.12 for secure electronic commerce on the Internet.
Internet Security 

     Digital Firewall for OpenVMS V1.0 prevents unauthorized access 
to and from the Internet and corporate networks.

     OpenVMS Internet Product Suite V1.0 also includes a rich 
collection of applications, development tools, news readers, 
graphics and video viewers, HTML utilities and conversion tools. 
The $99 price include all tools and freeware, plus trial licenses 
for all browser and server software. It is available this summer.

ALL-IN-1 Office Server V3.2 for OpenVMS

     ALL-IN-1 Office Server V3.2 for OpenVMS offers Internet 
document server capabilities without the need for HTML authoring 
tools or modification to ALL-IN-1 documents. Personal use licenses 
are priced from $135. The software is available immediately.
Delivering Integrated Enterprise Messaging

     The following products and services from Digital enable full 
integration of Windows-based mail systems with enterprise mail 
backbones.

MAILbus 400 Message Transfer Agent V2.0

     MAILbus 400 MTA V2.0 enables Microsoft Exchange servers to 
operate in a heterogeneous enterprise mail environment. The 
software supports the Exchange file transfer bodypart, enabling 
automatic conversion and exchange of mail messages between 
Exchange, Digital's ALL-IN-1 and MailWorks, and other mail
systems. MAILbus 400 MTA V2.0 is priced from $2,000 and is 
available immediately.

Digital X.500 Directory Services V3.0

     The newest version of Digital's X.500 Directory Services 
implements a distributed network directory that can support a 
worldwide population of mail users at faster-than-ever speeds, and 
automates synchronization with other directories. The X.500 
directory defines each recipient's profile, which, when used with 
the MAILbus 400 MTA, initiates document conversions automatically 
so that messages are delivered in each user's preferred format. 
Digital X.500 Directory Services V3.0 is priced from $500 and is 
available immediately.

MAILbus Monitor V2.0

     MAILbus Monitor V2.0 monitors messaging systems and network 
applications across LANs and WANs from a central location. It 
allows network managers to pinpoint and address problems quickly 
for uninterrupted message transfer.  MAILbus Monitor V2.0 is priced 
from $1,000 and is available immediately.

Support for Defense Messaging System Requirements

     Digital's suite of X.400 and X.500 messaging products will 
support the U.S. Department of Defense's Defense Messaging System 
(DMS) requirements for secure messaging. DMS support will encompass 
messaging products for OpenVMS, Windows NT and other platforms, and 
will be available for military and commercial customers.

Delivering Simplified C++ Development

     Digital is streamlining client/server development for the 
integrated OpenVMS and Windows NT environment with Application 
Developers Package for C++ V1.0.  This software product provides 
C/C++ developers with a model and process for building applications 
that run across OpenVMS and Windows NT servers and Windows 
desktops. Included are source code, executable images and complete
programming documentation. Application Developers Package for C++ 
V1.0 will be available in June on the World Wide Web.

     "These new products, together with our first wave of 
transaction processing and development products, give customers an 
abundant portfolio from which to draw for developing, deploying, 
integrating and managing bullet-proof business applications across 
Windows NT and OpenVMS," said Melling.

Delivering More Tools and Applications

     Since the initial announcement of Digital's OpenVMS and 
Windows NT integration program, the ISV community has responded 
continually to market demand for applications and tools that 
support the integrated environment.  Many products are shipping 
today and contributing to successful integration projects 
worldwide. The following software vendors added their support to
Digital's program today.

Client/Server Application Development Environments

     JYACC, Inc.			                  Powersoft
     Mainsoft                     Software		   Synergex
     ParcPlace - Digitalk, Inc.			     Visix Software

Applications

