              Digital Unveils New Pentium Pro Servers
              and Aggressively-Priced Desktop Computers
              
           --Enterprise customers get connected with new
             Windows NT and 64-bit computing solutions--

     WINDOWS WORLD/COMDEX, CHICAGO, June 3,1996 -- Digital 
Equipment Corporation today kicked-off Spring Windows World/COMDEX 
with several innovative new products and solutions, including Intel 
Pentium Pro-based Prioris ZX 6000 servers and the easy-to-own 
Venturis FX family of Pentium-based desktop systems.

     Continuing to strengthen Digital's award winning family of 
Prioris servers, the company today unveiled the new Prioris ZX 
6200MP and Prioris ZX 6166MP four-way Pentium Pro Symmetric 
Multiprocessing (SMP) PC servers, which bring new levels of 
functionality and price/performance to enterprise class computing.  
Based on either the 200- or 166MHz Pentium Pro microprocessors, the 
new Prioris ZX 6000 series offers mid-to-large commercial 
enterprises maximum performance for enterprise-wide applications 
that demand highly-available servers that are scaleable and 
manageable. Pricing for the new Prioris ZX 6000 series ranges from 
about U.S. $17,000 to about $34,000, based on configuration.

     In addition, Digital announced the immediate availability of 
the latest Pentium processor models of the Prioris LX, Prioris XL 
and Prioris ZX 5000 series servers. The Prioris ZX series delivers 
unprecedented reliability when used in concert with Digital 
Clusters for Windows NT Server software. Digital's 
recently-announced Clusters for Windows NT Server software takes 
advantage of industry-standard hardware to deliver the industry's 
highest system availability for file services and databases. 

     The company also announced the new Venturis FX family of 
Pentium-based desktop systems that offer customers reliable, 
price/performance leading computing solutions -- with prices 
starting at only U.S. $1,679 -- that are easy to own and maintain. 
With processing speeds ranging from 100- to 166MHz, the Venturis FX 
family delivers a broad range of cost-effective, yet powerful 
solutions to businesses of all sizes -- from customers who require 
entry-level personal productivity machines running Windows 95 to 
high-end power users who demand Windows NT on the desktop.

     "Digital is delivering on its strategy to provide customers 
with robust solutions centered on their needs," said Bruce Claflin, 
vice president and general manager of Digital's Personal Computer 
Business.  "Today's announcements clearly establish Digital as the 
right choice for Windows NT solutions.  We offer the broadest range 
of products, unmatched functionality, and excellent 
price/performance for customers deploying Windows NT across the 
enterprise."

OTHER RELATED DIGITAL ANNOUNCEMENTS AND ACTIVITIES AT SPRING 
WINDOWS WORLD/COMDEX THIS WEEK INCLUDE:

New AlphaServer 4100 systems:  

     Digital showcases the first affordable enterprise-class 
computing solution. The 64-bit RISC systems bring an 
industry-unique computing environment to both large enterprises and 
small companies, using Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, or Windows NT 
operating systems Digital will demonstrate two AlphaServer 4100s 
running Windows NT and the Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server 
software.

High-Performance Digital workstations running AccelPRO graphics 
subsystems: 

     The powerful combination of AccelGraphics' new high 
performance AccelPRO graphics subsystems and Digital's powerful 
NT-based Pentium Pro and Alpha workstations provides a compelling 
solution for visual computing and will be demonstrated in the 
Digital booth. 

     "The market is increasingly demanding high-performance 
solutions on Windows NT for professionals and we are pleased to be 
at the forefront of this trend with Digital as a key supplier of 3D 
Graphics.  We welcome this opportunity to further expand our 
relationship with Digital as we work together to bring 3D compute 
intensive solutions to satisfy and excite customers worldwide," 
said Jeffrey Dunn, President and CEO of AccelGraphics, Inc. 

LinkWorks V3.0 for Windows NT, Windows 95, Apple Macintosh and 
Motif:

     Version 3.0 includes significant enhancements and capabilities 
in client support. This version also brings one of the first 
solutions to market that offers solution providers and end users 
the advantages and benefits of distributed OLE (Object Linking and 
Embedding).  This release also includes the first phase of 
integrating Microsoft Exchange Mail Client with the LinkWorks 
framework.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

