 Digital Delivers Unparalleled Functionality and Performance to the
    Enterprise with New Intel Pentium Pro 200- and 166MHZ Servers

 New Prioris ZX 6000MP Series elevate the role of PC servers in the
 enterprise; company also unveils three new Intel Pentium models for 
                   its current Prioris server line

     MAYNARD, Mass., June 3, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the new Prioris ZX 6200MP and Prioris ZX6166MP 
four-way Pentium Pro Symmetric Multiprocessing (SMP) PC servers 
which bring new levels of functionality and price/performance to 
enterprise class computing.

     Based on either the 200- or 166MHz Pentium Pro microprocessors, 
the new Prioris ZX 6000 series are optimized for Windows NT Server 
software and offer mid-to-large commercial enterprises maximum 
performance for enterprise-wide applications that demand 
highly-available servers that are scaleable and manageable. 

     The company also announced the immediate availability of the 
latest Intel Pentium processor models of the Prioris LX, Prioris XL 
and Prioris ZX 5000 series servers.

     "Digital recognizes the importance of providing a robust server 
capable of supporting enterprise applications, such as databases, 
groupware and Internet access, and the Prioris ZX 6000 series 
unquestionably delivers the industry's most powerful PC-class 
solution," said Howard Elias, vice president, worldwide business 
segments for Digital's PC Business. "As always, the Prioris server 
family provides customers with a high-performance, reliable server 
solution by incorporating the fastest Intel Pentium and Pentium Pro 
processors. These systems, combined with the recently-announced 
Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server software, ensure that 
mission-critical business applications are continuously 
operational."  

     "The powerful combination of Digital's Prioris server systems 
with Windows NT Server and the Microsoft BackOffice family of server 
applications offers customers real business value through powerful, 
scaleable and highly-available solutions for business-critical 
applications," said Jim Allchin, senior vice president of the 
desktop and business systems division at Microsoft.
Industry Leading Performance: 

     The high-performance Prioris ZX 6000 series incorporates 
state-of-the-art dual peer PCI bus and four-way symmetrical 
multiprocessing, fault-resilient and rapid recovery hardware 
subsystems optimized for Windows NT Server.  As with all of 
Digital's award-winning Prioris PC servers, the Prioris ZX series 
delivers maximum investment longevity through balanced system 
design, a highly-expandable architecture, and robust 
fault-tolerance.  Furthermore, the Prioris ZX servers are certified 
for all leading industry-standard operating systems.

     "Digital and Intel have a long-standing relationship that has 
delivered a series of award-winning Prioris server products to the 
marketplace. The latest in this series, the Prioris ZX 6000 servers, 
combines a number of key elements into a package that is likely to 
win further awards," said Dave House, senior vice president and 
general manager of Intel's Enterprise Server Group. "Digital's 
innovative clustering and server-management technologies, combined 
with the affordability and power of the standard four-way Pentium 
Pro processor server is compelling. It really addresses the 
availability and cost-of-ownership concerns that are so critical to 
enterprise-level customers."
Windows NT Clusters for High Availability:

     The Prioris ZX series delivers unprecedented reliability when 
used in concert with Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server 
software. Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server software takes 
advantage of industry-standard hardware to deliver high-availability 
for file services and databases. 

     Digital's offering surpasses existing solutions on the market. 
Unlike competitive high-availability file servers, hardware is not 
left idle in standby mode; failover is transparent to users; 
Digital's unique failback feature allows scheduled maintenance to be 
performed without disruption; and the cluster is managed through a 
user-friendly graphical interface. 

System Scaleability: 

     The Prioris ZX 6000 series provides the power and throughput to 
handle the most demanding server applications through expandable 
processor, disk, memory and I/O subsystems as well as optional 
advanced RAID configurations. Features include expandability up to 
2GB of system memory and 12 I/O expansion slots - including 8 PCI 
and 4 EISA. This flexibility and expansion power helps protect 
customers' technology investments as resource-intensive multimedia 
database and high-traffic Internet/Intranet applications become more 
prevalent.

System Manageability: 

     Like all Prioris PC servers, each Prioris ZX 6000 server will 
include at no extra cost Digital's ServerWORKS Manager, an 
easy-to-use system and network management software package, and 
ServerWORKS Quick Launch, a CD-ROM suite of utilities that automates 
network operating system installation and the configuration of 
Digital Prioris PC servers including enhanced manageability features 
for Pentium Pro and Clustered servers. Digital's Remote Server 
Manager option provides out-of-band server management and control 
for remote or distributed sites with limited on-site LAN 
administration capabilities.  Additionally, Digital's rackmount 
option allows any combination of Prioris servers and external 
storage devices to be installed in a rack without modification to 
the systems' chassis or wiring. 

Intel Power Curve: 

     As another reflection of Digital's dedication to delivering the 
latest in Intel Pentium processor technology, the company introduced 
three new Prioris servers featuring Intel's 150- and 166MHz 
processors.  The latest models include the Prioris LX 5150, the 
Prioris XL 5166, and the Prioris ZX 5166 servers.
Pricing/Availability: 

     The Prioris ZX 6200MP will be available late Summer 1996.  The 
Prioris ZX 6166MP will be available in July of 1996.  Pricing for 
the new Pentium Pro Prioris ZX 6200MP server ranges from US $18,089 
to $33,749, based on configuration.  Pricing for the new Pentium Pro 
Prioris ZX 6166MP server ranges from US $17,069 to $32,249, based on 
configuration. 

