          Formation of Digital Services Division Announced

      Reinforces Company Position As One Of The World's Leading
            Providers of Integration Services and Support

MAYNARD, Mass., June 11, 1996 - Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the formation of the Digital Services Division that will 
focus on enterprise service solutions for large and medium-sized 
companies.

     "Today, customers seek service providers to help them in three 
important areas: integration of system and network-based solutions;
product service and interoperability support across a multivendor 
environment; and, management of much, if not all, of their 
information technology operations," said Digital Chairman Robert B. 
Palmer.  "These opportunities match our core service strengths and 
to take full advantage, we are forming a new Digital Services 
Division to better and more efficiently serve our customers."

     The new division will be made up of three business units: 
Operations Management Services; Systems Integration Services; and 
Multivendor Customer Services. It will be led by Digital Vice 
President John Rando who currently heads the company's Multivendor 
Customer Services organization.  

     Commenting on the new division, Rando said, "A key component of 
this new structure is the combining of our systems integration and 
network services operations into the Systems Integration Business 
Unit. This will allow us to manage our system integration business 
as a full portfolio of services directed toward network intensive 
business solutions and aligned with our corporate strategy of high 
performance 64-bit computing, Windows NT across the enterprise and 
Internet/Intranet."  

      The Operations Management Services Business Unit will focus on 
distributed data center management; enterprise application 
management; desk top management; and, Internet/Intranet management.  

     The Systems Integration Business Unit will focus on target 
application solutions including mail and messaging; electronic 
commerce; information management; enterprise applications;
manufacturing execution systems; and, telecom industry solutions.

     The Multivendor Customers Services Business Unit will provide 
the highest level of availability and interoperability support for 
complex, multivendor environments; focus on technical and 
operational excellence in UNIX, Windows NT and the Internet for 
mission-critical environments; provide total service event 
management; and, continue ongoing support for its current customer 
base. 

     The Digital Services Division will focus on enterprise service 
solutions for large to medium companies, will work with a select 
number of channel partners to meet the needs of the broader market 
for Digital services and with enterprise product vendors such as 
Compaq, Microsoft, and Computer Associates.

Realigned Selling Teams

     In other news, Digital announced that it is combining its 
systems sales and technical support in its Americas region as well 
as combining worldwide support operations for these functions. The 
company also is customizing sales coverage for its systems sales 
accounts in Europe.

     The company said the changes will provide a more efficient, 
consistent selling function while expanding direct coverage to more 
accounts. In addition, the alignment will take significant steps 
forward in strengthening relationships with channels partners and in 
satisfying customers, the company said.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
