                   Daily Southtown Selects Digital
            as Systems Integrator for Prepress Operations

                            NEXPO '96       
                           Booth # 1012

MAYNARD, Mass., June 17, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced that it has reached an agreement on a contract with The 
Daily Southtown to implement a fully integrated, client/server 
prepress solution in the newspaper's suburban Chicago facility.  The 
prepress solution will utilize three AlphaServer 1000 systems 
running Windows NT and Microsoft SQL in a high availability 
configuration.  

     Digital will integrate the news and advertising operation of 
the Daily Southtown with its sister paper, Star Publications, as the 
two newspapers consolidate operations into a new building located in 
southwest suburban Tinley Park, Illinois.  The combined operation 
will have 80 editorial seats, 21 editorial pagination seats, and 37 
classified seats.  

     Norm Rosinski, publisher of both papers, has experience working 
with Digital.  "In 1993, Digital integrated the news and advertising 
operations at Star Publications," said Rosinski.  "Because of the 
quality performance we've been able to achieve with their solutions, 
we selected Digital to work with us as we enter this new phase in 
our history." 

     The Daily Southtown has selected Sysdeco's DewarView for its 
new editorial and pagination system in the newsroom; CompuText's 
Compuclass 5.0 for its classified advertising and pagination system; 
and a library system.  As prime contractor, Digital will manage the 
hardware and software staging, project and cutover management, 
installation and support of third party and Digital components, as 
well as on-site application and system administration training.  

     Digital's unique implementation of the DewarView editorial 
system provides exceptional ease of use with Microsoft products, 
such as Windows 95, Word, and MS-Mail.  DewarView provides the tools 
needed to generate, receive, edit, route, store, and output newsroom 
information.  It also provides seamless integration with QuarkXPress 
for automated copy paste-up, layout, and page design.  Because of 
the system's capabilities, the quality of the editorial content and 
design can be greatly improved.  The system also allows for 
repurposing editorial information for electronic library systems and 
internet publishing.

     The CompuClass advertising system allows ad-takers, 
advertising, and production mangers to manage, track, and report 
revenue  Because of the system's unique rating, zoning, and 
upselling capabilities, newspapers can maximize their revenue while 
streamlining the production process.  CompuClass uses Microsoft 
Windows 95, Word, and Crystal Reports.

     The Daily Southtown and Star Publications are part of Hollinger 
International's Chicago group, which includes the Chicago Sun-Times 
and Pioneer Press, a 200,00 circulation paid weekly group serving 
Chicago's north and northwest suburbs. 

