        Digital Unveils New Venturis FX Family of Desktop PCs
        
                     Easy-to-Own systems deliver
          outstanding performance at industry leading prices

     MAYNARD, Mass., June 3, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the new Venturis FX family of Pentium-based desktop 
systems that offer customers reliable, price/performance leading 
computing solutions that are easy to own and maintain.

     With processing speeds ranging from 100MHz up to the 
soon-to-be-announced 200MHz, the Venturis FX family delivers a broad 
range of cost-effective, yet powerful solutions to businesses of all 
sizes from customers who require entry-level personal productivity 
machines running Windows 95 to high-end power users who demand 
Windows NT on the desktop.

     Further establishing Digital as an industry price/performance 
leader, pricing for the Venturis FX line begins at US $1,679 and the 
new systems will offer either Windows 95 or Windows NT configuration 
options.

     "In order to maintain a competitive edge, business customers 
need a computing solution that will grow with them as their needs 
change," said Howard Elias, vice president, worldwide business 
segments for Digital's PC Business.  "Not only are these powerful 
and aggressively-priced systems easier to upgrade, expand and 
manage, they also come with the Digital reputation of reliability, 
which gives customers the peace of mind that they have a solution 
they can depend on."

Increased Performance at Affordable Prices:

     By combining Digital's engineering expertise with the computing 
power of Intel's Pentium processor and industry-leading technology 
such as EDO memory, pipeline burst cache and--for maximum 
flexibility--the industrys only single socket memory upgrade path, 
the new Venturis FX systems deliver up to 20 percent greater 
performance than the previous generation of Venturis systems.  This 
performance increase--which allows customers to do more in less 
time--comes at no incremental cost to the customer over previous 
systems.

Easy to Own, Maintain and Use: 

     Digital is aware that maintaining and upgrading a system 
actually can be even more expensive than purchasing it. In response, 
Digital has developed a new enclosure and motherboard that serve to 
reduce the total cost of ownership for channel partners and 
customers.  

     With the newly designed and engineered enclosures, the Venturis 
FX family makes upgrading and servicing a PC quicker and easier than 
ever before.  The enclosure is tool-less and has only one thumb 
screw, which stays on the enclosure. There are no cables to the 
motherboard, so there is no need to unhook them during maintenance. 
The motherboard has no screws and quickly slides in and out on 
rails.  Because the most commonly-upgraded components have been 
moved to the front of the motherboard, away from the option slots, 
users can leave option cards in while upgrading the CPU, memory, 
video memory, and cache.  Getting the system up and running is also 
simple since the mouse and keyboard are color-coded for faster 
setup.

     In order to protect customers' hardware investments and stay on 
the cutting edge of the Intel power curve, the new Venturis FX 
family is designed for easy upgrade to faster Intel processors.  By 
incorporating the ZIF Socket 7 on the motherboard, customers can 
easily "snap" out the old processor chip and "snap" in the new one.
Easy to Manage: 

     For all of Digital's commercial desktop, server and mobile 
products, manageability is a key feature; Venturis FX is no 
exception.  Digital includes its latest industry-standard version of 
ClientWORKS manageability software on Venturis FX.  ClientWORKS 
helps manage users' assets and network, reducing the overall cost of 
ownership.  ClientWORKS adheres to the Desktop Management Task Force 
(DMTF) specifications, and has unique features, including a 32-bit 
service layer for Windows 95 and Windows NT compatibility, more 
component information, as well as dynamic BIOS recognition. What 
this all means to the customer is the most robust manageability in 
the industry, which reduces support costs and improves accuracy of 
analysis.  Best of all:  It comes free of charge.
Reliability: 

     The Venturis FX family has over 60 human years of testing 
behind every machine.  In addition, Digital designs and manufactures 
its own motherboards for the Venturis FX, allowing for improved 
performance and tighter quality control.  The systems also meet or 
exceed worldwide environmental health and safety guidelines for 
recyclable components, and the Energy Star certification.

Colorful World: 

     In response to extensive customer research, Digital is 
heralding the arrival of the Venturis FX family with a new, brighter 
color that better blends into todays corporate environment.  Digital 
is transitioning the Venturis FX peripherals and components to the 
new color, as well.  Digital will also incorporate the new color 
across the other desktop product families throughout the year.
Pricing/Availability: 

     The Venturis FX 5100 up to and including the Venturis FX 5166 
models are available immediately through Digital's channel partners 
including master resellers, wholesalers, distributors, dealers, VARs 
and system integrators.  Pricing for the new Venturis FX family 
ranges from US $1,679 to $2,789, based on configuration.  For 
complete pricing information and system configuration, please call 
1-800-DIGITAL.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
