      Prioris ZX, Venturis FX, HiNote, NT Clustering Technology
              Form Backbone of Enterprise-Wide Solution

NEW YORK, June 18, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
demonstrated its enterprise-wide technology solution at PC Expo 
(Booth #3734), showcasing new PC servers and desktop systems.  The 
Prioris ZX servers, Venturis FX desktop computers, HiNote notebooks 
and Digital Clusters for Windows NT software form the basis of 
Digital's exhibit and highlight the company's PC-based technology, 
which offers end users seamless connectivity and integration across 
the enterprise.

     The Prioris ZX servers are the latest in Digital's line of 
award-winning Prioris family of servers.  The recently introduced 
products include the Intel Pentium Pro-based Prioris ZX 6200MP and 
Prioris ZX 6166MP four-way Pentium Pro Symmetric Multiprocessing 
(SMP) PC servers, which bring new levels of functionality and 
price/performance to enterprise-class computing.  Based on either 
the 200- or 166MHz Pentium Pro microprocessors, the new Prioris ZX 
6000 series offers mid-to-large commercial enterprises maximum 
performance for enterprise-wide applications that demand highly 
available servers that are scalable and manageable.

     Also featured in the booth are Digital's new Venturis FX family 
of Pentium-based desktop systems, which were introduced earlier this 
month.  The new systems offer customers reliable, price/performance 
leading computing solutions that are easy to own and maintain.  With 
processing speeds from 100- to 200MHz, the Venturis FX family 
delivers a broad range of cost-effective yet powerful solutions to 
businesses of all sizes -- from customers who require entry-level 
personal productivity machines running Windows 95 to high-end power 
users who demand Windows NT on the desktop.

     Prominently showcased in the booth are Digital's award-winning 
HiNote notebooks.  The all Pentium line features 100- to 133MHz 
processors and includes several network-ready features that help 
network administrators get the most out of their networking 
environments.  The HiNote family is targeted at customers from the 
small business user to sophisticated, large business mobile 
professionals and includes the industry's first fully integrated 
Windows NT mobile clients.

     A major component of the booth is Digital Clusters for Windows 
NT Server software, which takes advantage of industry-standard 
hardware to deliver high availability for file services and 
databases.  This offering surpasses existing solutions on the 
market.  Unlike competitive high-availability files servers, 
hardware is not left idle in standby mode -- failover is transparent 
to users.  Digital's unique failback feature allows scheduled 
maintenance to be performed without disruption and the cluster is 
managed through a user-friendly graphical interface.  Digital offers 
the only cluster solution available for both Intel and RISC servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
