	  White Pine Strengthens Commitment to Digital's 
		     Windows NT Alpha Platform

... Ships Enhanced CU-SeeMe(tm) for Windows NT AlphaServer(tm) 
    systems ... Plans Alpha NT(tm) client support ... Joins Digital's 
    Internet Innovators Program ...

... Alpha powers White Pine's LIVE Internet Broadcasts at PC Expo ...

NEW YORK CITY, PC EXPO (June 18, 1996) - At a joint press briefing 
here today, White Pine Software, Inc., a leader in desktop 
videoconferencing, demonstrated its growing commitment to Digital 
Equipment Corporation's high-performance Windows NT Alpha computing 
platform.

White Pine and Digital executives announced the following 
developments in White Pine's growing relationship with Digital, 
including:

o Immediate availability of Enhanced CU-SeeMe Reflector server 
software, a leading client/server desktop videoconferencing 
technology for the Internet and Intranet, for Digital's Windows NT 
based AlphaServer systems.

o Plans to port Enhanced CU-SeeMe client software for to the Windows 
NT Alpha-based workstation platforms.

o Membership in Digital's Internet Innovator's program through which 
White Pine and Digital are developing a multifaceted relationship to 
jointly promote and market Internet and Intranet focused solutions.

In addition, the companies used PC Expo as an opportunity to 
showcase the new technologies announced today, including a live 
Internet videoconference with US troops stationed in Bosnia, live 
conferencing between Digital and Microsoft booths, and, a live 
broadcast of Scott McNealy's keynote address over the Internet, all 
powered by Enhanced CU-SeeMe and the superior performance of NT 
AlphaServer systems.

Enhanced CU-SeeMe and the White Pine Reflector has quickly grown to 
the technology of choice for desktop videoconferencing over the 
Internet and Intranet. Enhanced CU-SeeMe provides person-to-person 
conferencing, group conferencing and live broadcasting using TCP/IP 
over POTS, ISDN, LAN and the Internet. Commitment to Digital's 
Windows NT Alpha platforms, industry standards and increased 
interoperability will further deliver CU-SeeMe into the corporate 
Intranet market.

"Enhanced CU-SeeMe for Digital's NT Alpha platforms delivers the 
power of desktop videoconferencing to a broad set of commercial and 
business users, including ISPs and content providers," said Jack 
Dutzy, vice president of marketing and strategic sales for White 
Pine Software. "White Pine's videoconferencing software combined 
with Digital's worldwide reach and leadership in the Windows NT 
environment will enable customers worldwide to communicate and 
conduct business more effectively within their own company or across 
the globe."

Digital NT Alpha customers will have greater access to the 
industry's most popular videoconferencing software solutions. With 
Enhanced CU-SeeMe technology, Digital customers can conduct 
real-time audio and video conferencing over the Internet and private 
TCP/IP networks, as well as live broadcasting ("cybercasting").

"Our customers tell us how excited they are about the Enhanced 
CU-SeeMe/Alpha/NT ensemble," said Nancy Epple, Digital's AlphaServer 
marketing director. "Enhanced CU-SeeMe on our breakthrough Alpha NT 
platforms provides an intriguing offering of both Internet and 
Intranet business solutions for the SOHO market, telecommuters, ISPs 
and organizations worldwide."

The Internet AlphaServer family features preconfigured hardware and 
software packages designed to make Internet and Web access, 
navigation, and management easy. Prepackaged software and 
preconfigured systems are designed to minimize the effort and time 
associated with getting users active and productive on the Internet.

"We are very pleased to have White Pine as an Internet Innovator," 
said Joan Jacobs, strategic relations manager for Digital's Internet 
Business Group. "White Pine's leadership technology in Internet 
based videoconferencing, and their aggressive go-to-market approach 
to applying the technology in Internet/Intranet applications, 
exemplifies the type of cutting edge company that Digital is looking 
to partner with in this program."

Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open client 
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scaleable Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

With Enhanced CU-SeeMe client/server technology, customers can 
expect to communicate in new and exciting ways over the Internet, 
regardless of their computer platform or operating system. White 
Pine Software is a leader in desktop videoconferencing over the 
Internet, and provides desktop connectivity solutions for Microsoft 
Windows, Macintosh and ALPHA- and UNIX-based platforms. For more 
information visit http://www.cu-seeme.com, email info@wpine.com or 
call 603-886-9050.

