                EC Prokopis Joins IONA Technologies

CAMBRIDGE, Mass. -- June 24, 1996 -- CORBA market leader IONA 
Technologies has announced the appointment of E.C. "Mick" Prokopis, 
53, as chief operating officer and chief financial officer, 
effective July 1. Prokopis joins IONA Technologies from Digital 
Equipment Corporation, where he held the position of vice president 
and corporate controller.

IONA Technologies, a privately held software firm, develops and 
markets Orbix, the leading product in the CORBA (Common Object 
Request Broker Architecture) marketplace. CORBA is the standard set 
by the Object Management Group which allows for cross platform 
integration of software components and applications regardless of 
how, where or when they are implemented.

Currently staffed by 120 people, with offices in Cambridge, 
Massachusetts, Dublin, Ireland and Perth, Western Australia, IONA 
grew by more than 300 percent last year. Orbix sells primarily to 
Fortune 1000 corporations, telecommunication providers, government 
departments and independent software vendors around the world. 

In welcoming Prokopis to IONA, president and chief executive officer 
Dr. Chris Horn said, "We are thrilled to have Mick join our senior 
management team. IONA has experienced exponential sales and revenue 
increases over the last few years. Mick's experience and talents 
will help the company continue to execute its plans for expansion."

Digital's Chief Financial Officer Vin Mullarkey praised Prokopis for 
his judgment, leadership and contributions. "Mick provided 
outstanding leadership and performance during a very critical time 
in Digital's history," Mullarkey said. "We will miss his talent and 
his energy, but we certainly wish him well with this new 
opportunity."

At IONA, Prokopis will be responsible for consolidating and 
extending the company's impressive growth. "IONA offers an exciting 
new opportunity for me. I am attracted by the company's record since 
its founding in 1991, the strength of its Orbix product line and the 
caliber and vision of the existing management team. I plan to play a 
key role in the further development of the company," said Prokopis.

"As the distributed object technology standard CORBA is one of the 
most important advances in software development this decade. IONA's 
Orbix already has a strong lead in the field and is changing the 
structure of the software industry. I look forward to being part of 
the company that is driving this exciting technology," added 
Prokopis.

Prokopis has extensive experience in the computer industry. He 
joined Digital after holding executive-level positions at the Ziff
Corporation, Lotus Development Corporation, and United Technologies
Corporation. He holds a bachelor's degree from the University of 
Massachusetts, Amherst.

IONA Technologies is the world's leading provider of CORBA 
conforming solutions. Its principal product, Orbix, was launched in 
June 1993. With Orbix, corporate developers can develop and 
integrate distributed, applications based on new and existing 
software components.

Orbix currently runs on 20 different operating systems from Windows 
and UNIX to MVS and selected real time platforms. Orbix is also 
integrated with a wide range of third-party software products and is 
used in more than 1000 organizations around the world. 

