                Citibank Chooses Digital to Implement
               Worldwide Client/Server Infrastructure

  Digital Wins $500M Global Deal for Desktop and LAN Technologies 
                                  	
MAYNARD, Mass., June 25, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced it has been awarded a three-year, $500M deal by 
Citibank to implement, service and support a large portion of 
Citicorp's desktop and local-area networking (LAN) systems and 
software throughout the world.

     According to the agreement, Digital will provide PC hardware, 
software and networking support to Citicorp via a monthly payment 
plan.  This innovative fee-for-services arrangement allows Citicorp 
to manage for constant change and take full advantage of new 
technology.  It will also enable Citicorp to better manage its 
worldwide desktop costs.

     Representing one of the largest contracts ever awarded for 
global desktop and LAN management, the agreement is part of the 
implementation of Project Enterprise, which is Citibank's plan to 
standardize Citicorp LANs and desktops on a common hardware and 
software platform.  Under the contract, Digital will implement the 
largest portion of Citibank's rollout of this global client/server 
infrastructure.

     According to John Rando, vice president and general manager of 
Digital's Services division, "Digital's global reach and wide range 
of client/server management services were key to winning this 
business.  "In addition," added Rando, "this contract represents a 
significant change in the way global corporations choose to manage 
their information systems.  While most large IT management solutions 
have focused on mainframe data centers, our strategic solution for 
Citicorp -- which is based on Digital's award-winning PC Utility 
program -- has concentrated on the need to effectively manage 
desktop computing environments.  That is the segment of the 
enterprise where the most dynamic change occurs, and where worldwide 
standardization and consistent management can reap the greatest 
benefits for global corporations."

     "We worked closely with Digital throughout the pilot phase of 
Project Enterprise to validate our desktop computing strategy," said 
Ranjit Singh, head of Project Enterprise and vice president of 
Global Distributed Computing and LANs for Citibank.  "The experience 
gave us confidence that Digital's global service delivery infra-
structure and multivendor expertise would provide us the necessary 
resources to successfully roll out a consistent, standards-
compliant, client/server computing platform for Citibankers around 
the world."

     Project Enterprise is Citibank's solution to understand and 
manage technology change, especially at the desktop and LAN platform 
level. By integrating the bank's processes, Citibank is able to 
manage its technology assets more efficiently and build an enabling 
infrastructure for introducing technological innovation.  Under terms of 
the contract, Digital's Multivendor Customer Services division will 
deliver total lifecycle desktop services including:

     *	Assessment and design of network and desktop systems
     *	PC, server, hub, router, software and structured wiring 
        procurement 
     *	Installation, upgrade and migration of network and end-user 
        systems 
     *	End-user orientation and ongoing training
     *	Comprehensive help desk (problem resolution & change 
        management)
     *	Remote monitoring, systems management and LAN operations
     *	Software license management
     *	Periodic hardware and software refresh
     *	Remedial and preventive maintenance 

     As the technology landscape changes, Digital will also work 
with Citibank to adapt the infrastructure and prepare the global 
workplace for continuing innovation. 

     Citicorp is a global financial services organization serving 
consumers, corporations and financial institutions through a network 
of over 3,400 offices and branches in over 90 countries and 
territories, spanning the developed and emerging economies of the 
world.  Citicorp's key competitive advantage--an unmatched global 
network, a commitment to customer satisfaction, and an edge through 
application of technology--plus the dedication to continuous 
improvement and innovation, distinguishes Citibank as a uniquely 
global bank.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

